Microsoft Entra ID - User Provisioning

1. Objective

The objective of this lab is to understand how user accounts and groups are managed in Microsoft Entra ID.

The lab focuses on creating users, assigning group membership, and understanding the relationship between identities and access.

2. Environment

Platform: Microsoft Entra ID

Environment: Personal lab / test tenant

Tools: Microsoft Entra admin center

User accounts: Fictional test identities

3. Tasks Performed

Created a test user.

Created a security group.

Assigned the test user to the group.

Reviewed the user's properties and group membership.

Verified the configuration.

4. Results

The test user was successfully created and assigned to the security group.

The lab demonstrated how group-based access management can be used to organize identities and manage access.

